--- !u!114 &381854128
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 381854127}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 53f0a0970cc466549bd79cfde54250cb, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  ending: {fileID: 1000915438}
  endingText: {fileID: 848966161}
  healthbarUI: {fileID: 176591595}
  dialogueLines:
  - "\u2026\u2026Is this\u2026 a hospital?"
  - The girl slowly opened her eyes, her vision still blurred, and the first thing
    that reached her ears was the faint hum of medical machines.
  - She lay quietly in the hospital bed, her breathing so light it felt like snow
    in early spring, not yet fully melted.
  - It was as if she had finally risen to the surface after drifting in a dream that
    had stretched on for far too long.
  - "That forest in the dream, those shadows, that long and silent battle\u2014they
    receded inch by inch, like the tide pulling away."
  - So it had not been entirely a dream.
  - "The shadow that had always stood in her way, the one she had called the \u201CDark
    Lord,\u201D was not truly some monster at all\u2014it was the illness that had
    kept her trapped in that coma for so long."
  - They had faced each other for what felt like an eternity, until at last, she
    broke free.
  - "\u201CDoctor, she\u2019s awake!\u201D"
  - "\u201CDon\u2019t rush, slowly\u2026 yes, she\u2019s responding.\u201D"
  - "\u201CThank goodness. You\u2019re finally awake.\u201D"
  - The girl stared quietly at the ceiling, as if she was still trying to make sense
    of the shape of the world around her.
  - "But she knew this much\u2014she had finally walked out of that endless darkness."
